From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_BIG_UPLOAD_CHUNK_RELEASE=1, a chunked image upload of over 64 MiB gives each chunk's staging buffer back once its copy is done (off by default)

Why: the 12288x12288 D16 shadow map (288 MiB) of the load past the field is uploaded in nine 32 MiB
chunks (TextureCache::UploadInChunks), each from a staging buffer of its own handed out in the same
tick, so all nine are held until the GPU is past that tick: in the load frame that is the next drain
(276 MiB of staging in run1545's drain 12, 240-276 MiB in other starts), at the moment the pool is at
zero.

What, with EDEN_UP_BIG_UPLOAD_CHUNK_RELEASE=1 (exact "1", read once at the texture cache's start):
- texture_cache/texture_cache.h (BigUploadChunkRelease, UploadStagingForChunk, ChunkGiveBack,
  UploadInChunks): for an image of over 64 MiB, every chunk but the last takes its staging buffer as a
  deferred one. Once the chunk's copy is recorded, TextureCacheRuntime::FinishChunkUpload submits and
  waits for the GPU (TextureCacheRuntime::Finish), carries what this tick handed out to the next tick
  (StagingBufferPool::CarryTick, as the ASTC transcode wait does: the draw being set up reads its
  uniforms in the new tick) and gives the buffer back as finished (FreeDeferred(ref, true)), so the next
  chunk takes the same buffer. The last chunk, and any chunk the pool has no deferred buffer for, goes
  the old way (UploadStagingNow). The copies, their order and barriers are unchanged; only the
  submissions between chunks are new, as the stream ring's WaitForStream already makes inside a draw's
  setup.
- renderer_vulkan/vk_texture_cache.h/.cpp: TextureCacheRuntime::FinishChunkUpload (a call to the
  existing Finish(), not a new scheduler.Wait/Finish line: the cost copy's wait-site count is T185's).
Lines (stderr): at boot "EDEN_UP_BIG_UPLOAD_CHUNK_RELEASE on: an image upload of over 64 MiB in chunks
submits and waits after each chunk but the last, and the next chunk takes the same staging buffer"; per
such upload (first 32, then every 32nd) "EDEN_UP_BIG_UPLOAD_CHUNK_RELEASE upload N: gpu=0x... WxH M MiB
in C chunks, G given back after their copy (W ms in those submits and waits), O the old way; staging
held at most H MiB instead of A MiB (S MiB less); T MiB less so far; frame=F". H and A are the chunks'
staging requests added up, not the pool's rounded buffer sizes.

Unset: one compare per chunked upload and one switch read at the texture cache's start; every chunk
calls UploadStagingNow as T185: as T185. No translation id input is touched (texture_cache.h and
vk_texture_cache.* are not reached from src/shader_recompiler or in the SINGLE list), no wait site line
is added, no anchor line changes, and the name is not in TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
